<title>JAPAN: Japan Jan chain store sales rise 0.8 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan Jan chain store sales rise 0.8 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sales at chain stores in Japan in January rose 0.8 percent year-on-year to 1.46 trillion yen, the Japan Chain Stores Association said on Monday.  </p>
<p>Month-on-month, chain store sales marked a 22.0 percent fall in January.</p>
<p>Sales of winter clothing and heating equipment slowed in January due to unusually high temperatures, the association said.</p>
<p>Prices of vegetables were on a falling trend, it said.</p>
</text>
